   $q$Triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $XYZ$. The measure of $\angle B$ is $(3x + 10)^\circ$ and the measure of $\angle Y$ is $(5x - 20)^\circ$. What is the measure of $\angle B$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$125^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-supplement-of-angle"},{"text":"$25^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-instead-of-added-when-solving"},{"text":"$15^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-x-instead-of-angle"},{"text":"$55^\\circ$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$55^\circ$$q$, $q$$\angle B$ and $\angle Y$ are corresponding angles, so $3x + 10 = 5x - 20$. Then $30 = 2x$ and $x = 15$. So $\angle B = 3(15) + 10 = 55^\circ$. The value $15^\circ$ is $x$, not the angle.$q$, 'draft', null)
