  ('9bc7d40e-9fed-59e7-b010-c7809b706887', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'triangle-congruence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Triangle $ABC$ has vertices $A(1, 2)$, $B(4, 2)$, and $C(1, 6)$. It is reflected across the $y$-axis to form triangle $A'B'C'$. What is the length of $B'C'$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$7$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-leg-lengths"},{"text":"$10$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-reflection-doubles-length"},{"text":"$3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-a-different-side"},{"text":"$5$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$5$$q$, $q$A reflection is a rigid motion, so $B'C' = BC$. From $B(4, 2)$ to $C(1, 6)$ the horizontal change is $3$ and the vertical change is $4$, so $BC = \sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = \sqrt{25} = 5$. The value $7$ adds the changes instead of using the Pythagorean theorem.$q$, 'draft', null)
