   $q$A translation maps triangle $PQR$ onto triangle $STU$, with $P$ going to $S$, $Q$ to $T$, and $R$ to $U$. In triangle $PQR$, $PQ = 6$ and $\angle Q = 48^\circ$. Which statement must be true?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$ST = 12$ and $\\angle T = 48^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-translation-stretches-lengths"},{"text":"$ST = 6$ and $\\angle U = 48^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"matched-angle-to-wrong-vertex"},{"text":"$ST = 6$ and $\\angle T = 48^\\circ$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$TU = 6$ and $\\angle T = 48^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"matched-side-to-wrong-vertices"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$ST = 6$ and $\angle T = 48^\circ$$q$, $q$A translation keeps lengths and angles. Side $PQ$ maps to side $ST$, so $ST = 6$, and $\angle Q$ maps to $\angle T$, so $\angle T = 48^\circ$. Side $TU$ is the image of $QR$, not $PQ$.$q$, 'draft', null)
