  ('e223fef8-4e6c-5f7d-9092-d0c55ae72d18', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'triangle-congruence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Triangle $ABC$ is congruent to triangle $DEF$. The side lengths are $AB = 2x + y$, $BC = x + 3y$, $DE = 11$, $EF = 13$, and $DF = 8$. What are the values of $x$ and $y$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x = 4$ and $y = 3$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$x = 5$ and $y = 1$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"matched-to-wrong-side"},{"text":"$x = 1$ and $y = 9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"satisfied-only-one-equation"},{"text":"$x = 3$ and $y = 4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-the-values"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x = 4$ and $y = 3$$q$, $q$By CPCTC, $AB = DE$ and $BC = EF$, so $2x + y = 11$ and $x + 3y = 13$. From the first equation, $y = 11 - 2x$. Substituting gives $x + 33 - 6x = 13$, so $x = 4$ and $y = 3$. Check: $2(4) + 3 = 11$ and $4 + 3(3) = 13$. The pair $x = 5$ and $y = 1$ sets $BC$ equal to $DF = 8$, but $BC$ corresponds to $EF$.$q$, 'draft', null)
